{"step_index":77,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T03:36:21Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T09:06:21+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T09:06:21+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_similar_channels.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 7516\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_similar_channels\",\"description\":\"Find COMPETITORS of a channel — either the user's own channel or a specific named channel. Uses neural semantic search tuned for competitor matching; the user's own authorized channels are automatically excluded from legacy manual-mode results.\\n\\nUse this tool ONLY when someone asks for competitors or similar channels relative to a channel:\\n- \\\"Who are my competitors?\\\" or \\\"Find channels like mine\\\" (the user's own channel — country/language are auto-detected in manual mode)\\n- \\\"Channels similar to [channel]\\\", \\\"Competitors of [channel]\\\", or \\\"Channels like @handle\\\" (a named reference channel)\\n\\nDo NOT use this tool for generic channel discovery by topic, size, growth, or any other criteria (\\\"find tech review channels\\\", \\\"top gaming channels in Brazil\\\", \\\"fastest growing fitness channels\\\") — use vidiq_channel_search for that.\\n\\nChoose exactly one mode: channelId or niche.\\n\\nADDITIVE CHANNEL ID MODE — when a canonical YouTube channel ID beginning with UC was supplied or already resolved, pass only channelId, plus optional size and sort. Do not copy resolved channel characteristics into this request or add niche/manual filters. Do not call vidiq_channel_search when a canonical ID is already available. A handle or URL must be resolved externally to a canonical channel ID before using this mode. The API derives the source classification and search tuning and excludes the reference channel.\\n\\nLEGACY MANUAL NICHE MODE — Legacy manual niche behavior is unchanged. The niche parameter is required in this mode — always provide a clear topic or content theme. All existing manual inputs remain supported, including minSubscribers, maxSubscribers, avgViews, avgViewsMin, avgViewsMax, country, language, channelType, faceless, and excludeChannelIds.\\n\\nSIMILAR TO A SPECIFIC CHANNEL IN LEGACY MANUAL MODE — when using the existing manual path, do NOT guess the reference channel's characteristics. Supply the same fields as before:\\n- niche: the reference channel's niche + subNiches, comma-separated (e.g. 'YouTube Growth, Monetization \\u0026 SEO')\\n- country: the reference channel's country\\n- language: the first code from the reference channel's languages\\n- channelType: the reference channel's channelType\\n- faceless: the reference channel's isFaceless value\\n- minSubscribers / maxSubscribers: a band around its subscriberCount, roughly 10% as min and 5x as max, unless the user asks for a specific range\\n- avgViews: the reference channel's avgViews; do not also set avgViewsMin/avgViewsMax unless the user asks for a specific range\\n- excludeChannelIds: the reference channel's channelId\\n\\nOmit sort for normal similarity ranking. When the user asks to rank these competitors by size or recent growth, set sort to subscriberCount, subsGrowth30d, or viewsGrowth30d; all explicit sorts reorder only the requested top similarity results.\\n\\nResults include the metrics used for sorting plus channel type and faceless status. In manual niche mode, country is a ranking preference rather than a strict filter, while language filters the language channels publish in. When omitted, country and language are auto-detected from the user's authorized channel.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"avgViews\":{\"description\":\"The reference channel's lifetime average views per video (total views / total videos). When searching for competitors of a specific channel, pass its avgViews here so results are auto-ranged to a similar per-video-views league (parallels passing the reference channel's subscriber band). Leave unset for generic niche searches.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"avgViewsMax\":{\"description\":\"Manual upper bound for lifetime average views per video (total views / total videos), overriding the avgViews auto-range. Use together with avgViewsMin to define a specific per-video average-views range.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"avgViewsMin\":{\"description\":\"Manual lower bound for lifetime average views per video (total views / total videos), overriding the avgViews auto-range. Use to require results that average at least this many views per video — e.g. 50000 for '50k+ average views'. This is the per-video average, not total views.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"channelId\":{\"description\":\"Canonical YouTube channel ID beginning with UC. It is passed directly to the Similar Channels API without a resolution request.\",\"pattern\":\"^UC[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"channelType\":{\"description\":\"Reference channel format. 'long' prefers long and mixed candidates; 'short' prefers short and mixed candidates; 'mixed' is neutral. This affects ranking, not eligibility.\",\"enum\":[\"long\",\"short\",\"mixed\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"country\":{\"description\":\"Two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code used to prefer channels BASED IN that country — e.g. 'US', 'GB', 'BR', 'JP'. Matching channels receive a ranking boost, but channels based elsewhere may still appear. This is where the channel is located — NOT the audience/viewer country, and NOT the channel's language (use `language` to filter by language). When omitted, the country is auto-detected from the user's authorized channel (if any).\",\"maxLength\":2,\"minLength\":2,\"type\":\"string\"},\"excludeChannelIds\":{\"description\":\"Manual niche mode only: channel IDs to exclude from results. The user's own authorized channels are excluded automatically and do not need to be listed.\",\"items\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":50,\"type\":\"array\"},\"faceless\":{\"description\":\"Reference channel faceless status. When provided, candidates with the same status receive a ranking boost; other candidates remain eligible.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"language\":{\"description\":\"Two-letter ISO 639-1 language code to filter results to channels whose content is in that language — e.g. 'en', 'es', 'pt', 'ja'. Pass the user's requested content language here (the language the channel publishes in — this is the channel's language, not its country). Only a single language is accepted. When omitted, the language is auto-detected from the user's authorized channel (if any).\",\"maxLength\":2,\"minLength\":2,\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxSubscribers\":{\"description\":\"Upper bound for subscriber count. Use to filter out larger channels — e.g. 1000000 to cap results at channels under 1M subscribers. Use together with minSubscribers to define a specific range.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"minSubscribers\":{\"description\":\"Lower bound for subscriber count. Use to filter out smaller channels — e.g. 10000 to only see channels with 10k+ subscribers. Use together with maxSubscribers to define a specific range.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"niche\":{\"description\":\"Manual niche, topic, or content theme to search in. Use natural language — e.g. 'tech reviews' or 'vegan cooking tutorials'. Provide either this or channelId, not both; prefer channelId for a specific reference channel.\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"size\":{\"default\":30,\"description\":\"Number of similar channels to return. Defaults to 30, maximum 50.\",\"maximum\":50,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"sort\":{\"description\":\"Optional descending sort of the requested top similarity results: subscriberCount, subsGrowth30d, or viewsGrowth30d. Omit to keep neural similarity relevance order.\",\"enum\":[\"subscriberCount\",\"subsGrowth30d\",\"viewsGrowth30d\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
